   <cell width="176">
    <color r="255" g="255" b="255">
     <font name="Gulim" size="12" shadowx="2" shadowy="1" shadowa="50">Fun Silky Shark Facts</font>
    </color>
   </cell>
   <p />
   <cell width="280" bgimg="ui/zoopedia/factBG.tga" padx="10">
    <p />
    <cell width="32" pady="10">
     <img src="ui/zoopedia/fact-bullet.tga" sx="0" sy="0" sw="32" sh="32" />
    </cell>
    <cell width="202" pady="10">
     <color r="255" g="255" b="255"><font name="Gulim" size="10">Silky sharks are not generally dangerous to divers, but in the presence of speared fish or if approached directly they can become aggressive, and therefore should be considered a potentially dangerous shark.

</font></color>
    </cell>
	<cell width="32" pady="10">
		<img src="ui/zoopedia/fact-bullet.tga" sx="0" sy="0" sw="32" sh="32" />
	</cell>    
    <cell width="202" pady="10">
     <color r="255" g="255" b="255"><font name="Gulim" size="10">It feeds mainly on inshore and pelagic bony fishes, but also eats squid and pelagic crab.</font></color>
    </cell>
	<cell width="32" pady="10">
		<img src="ui/zoopedia/fact-bullet.tga" sx="0" sy="0" sw="32" sh="32" />
	</cell>        
    <cell width="202" pady="10">
     <color r="255" g="255" b="255"><font name="Gulim" size="10">The maximum size is 3.3 m, but the length is usually not more than 2.4 m. </font></color>    
